# Accelerometer calibration (the six-pose), for the Lucid H7's two IMUs
#
# What a successful accel cal writes, read off AP_InertialSensor::_acal_save_calibrations()
# (ArduPilot master): per accel, INS_ACCnOFFS, INS_ACCnSCAL, INS_ACCn_CALTEMP and the
# device id; and, with INS_TRIM_OPTION 1 ("Assume first orientation was level"), AHRS_TRIM
# from the gravity direction in the first pose.
#
# INS_ACC_ID / INS_ACC2_ID are deliberately NOT pinned, for the same reason COMPASS_DEV_ID
# is not in gps-compass.param: the cal saves the id of the part detected on that boot. A
# value that is displayed is not necessarily saved -- the boot code sets the detected id
# without saving it, and the calibration counts only if the id loads from storage
# (AP_InertialSensor.cpp, _accel_id_ok) -- so restoring offsets alone does not clear
# "3D Accel calibration needed" after a parameter wipe. A six-pose saves the ids.
#
# provenance: six-pose on 2026-10-24 under 4.7.2, export in #600 (73938ae). Replaces the
# 2026-09-23 values restored by #596, which the FC would not accept because the ids had
# not been saved since the 2026-09-30 wipe.
#
# AHRS_TRIM is from Calibrate Level (which writes only AHRS_TRIM) on 2026-10-25, with the
# airframe level both side to side and fore-and-aft: X 0.43 deg, Y 0.45 deg. The
# six-pose's first pose, fore-and-aft unchecked, had set Y to -4.34 deg.
#   provenance: export in #603 (e0f7057)
INS_ACCOFFS_X,-0.007271941
INS_ACCOFFS_Y,0.02858531
INS_ACCOFFS_Z,-0.009277901
INS_ACCSCAL_X,0.9988925
INS_ACCSCAL_Y,0.9992484
INS_ACCSCAL_Z,1.001844
INS_ACC1_CALTEMP,57.36715
INS_ACC2OFFS_X,0.01243374
INS_ACC2OFFS_Y,0.04553617
INS_ACC2OFFS_Z,-0.06388364
INS_ACC2SCAL_X,0.9979284
INS_ACC2SCAL_Y,0.9997893
INS_ACC2SCAL_Z,0.9991022
INS_ACC2_CALTEMP,56.40097
AHRS_TRIM_X,0.007504338
AHRS_TRIM_Y,0.007802457
AHRS_TRIM_Z,0
